.TH DHISCTL 8
.SH NAME
dhisctl \- Diablo program to inspect and change dhistory entries
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dhisctl
[
.B \-e
|
.B \-u
]
[
.B \-f
.I file
]
[
.B \-h
]
[
.B \-p
]
[
.B \-S
]
[
.BR \-v [\fIn\fP]
]
[
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
]
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
[
.B \-V
]
.I historyfile
[
.I message-id
|
.I hash
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I dhisctl
works on a Diablo history file (normally dhistory in path_db).  It can
show the file's header and sizes, and mark single entries as expired or
clear that mark.
.PP
An entry is given as a Message-ID in angle brackets, or as its history
hash in the form
.IR h1 . h2
(two hexadecimal numbers, as printed by
.IR dilookup (8)).
More entries can be listed in a file with
.BR \-f .
Without
.B \-e
or
.B \-u
the entries are only looked up.
.PP
Expiring an entry this way only sets the expired mark in history; it
does not remove the article from the spool.  Use
.IR dcancel (8)
for that.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-e
Mark the entries as expired.
.TP
.B \-u
Clear the expired mark of the entries.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Read Message-IDs or hashes from \fIfile\fP, one per line, or from
standard input if \fIfile\fP is '-'.
.TP
.B \-h
Print the history header (magic, hash table size, version, entry and
header size) and the total size and number of entries.
.TP
.B \-p
Show progress on standard output.
.TP
.B \-S
Print the sizes of the internal history structures and the hash table
size from diablo.config, and exit.  No history file is needed.
.TP
.BR \-v [\fIn\fP]
Be more verbose: report each entry that is (un)expired or already was.
.TP
.BR \-d [\fIn\fP]
Set the debug level.
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default.
.TP
.B \-V
Print the version and exit.
.PP
.B \-a
(a scan of all entries) is no longer supported and is refused.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
dhisctl -h /news/dhistory
dhisctl -e -v /news/dhistory '<abc@example.com>'
dhisctl -u -f - /news/dhistory < message-ids
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
dilookup(8),
dcancel(8),
dhisexpire(8),
didump(8),
diablo-files(5)
